---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const GH = 'https://github.com/mxskeen/fudge';
---
<Base title="Install: Fudge" description="Build Fudge from source on Linux or macOS. Packages are planned.">
  <article class="page">
    <h1>Install</h1>
    <p class="lead">Fudge is pre-alpha and has no downloads yet. Today you build it from source.</p>

    <h2>Build from source</h2>
    <p>On Debian or Ubuntu, install the build dependencies and compile.</p>
<pre><code>sudo apt install build-essential pkg-config libgtk-4-dev libadwaita-1-dev \
  libgtk4-layer-shell-dev libsqlite3-dev libx11-dev libxcb1-dev
git clone {GH}.git
cd fudge
cargo build --release</code></pre>
    <p>You need a recent stable Rust toolchain from rustup. Then run it.</p>
<pre><code>./target/release/fudge          # start the daemon
./target/release/fudge toggle   # show or hide
./target/release/fudge query "72 f to c" --json</code></pre>
    <h3>macOS</h3>
    <p>Untested. This is the build as the README describes it. If it differs on your system, please open an issue.</p>
<pre><code>brew install gtk4 libadwaita pkg-config
cargo build --release</code></pre>

    <h2>Packages</h2>
    <p>Planned, none available yet: .deb, .rpm, AUR, Nix flake, AppImage, Homebrew cask and .dmg. Flatpak is deferred because its sandbox blocks ending processes and controlling windows.</p>

    <h2>The hotkey</h2>
    <p>The default is Alt Space, and it is configurable.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>X11.</strong> Grabbed directly.</li>
      <li><strong>Wayland.</strong> Planned through the GlobalShortcuts portal. Until then, bind <code>fudge toggle</code> to a key in your desktop.</li>
      <li><strong>macOS.</strong> Planned. Alt Space, which leaves Cmd Space to Spotlight.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>On Hyprland, add <code>bind = ALT, SPACE, exec, fudge toggle</code>. On Sway, add <code>bindsym Mod1+space exec fudge toggle</code>.</p>

    <h2>Uninstall</h2>
    <p>Delete the binary and the data folders listed on the <a href="../privacy/">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
